WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:11.870
[Narrator:] This is the virus, a tiny organism
less than one millionth of an inch in diameter,

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:17.340
magnified here thousands of times by the electron
microscope.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.260
This, the disease caused by the virus.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.230
One which has plagued man since recorded history.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.500
This, the scientist, Dr. John Enders of Harvard,

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:37.430
whose work made possible an effective vaccine
which can prevent the disease.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
This, the place where the vaccine is tested
and produced

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:47.730
for use throughout the world. West Point,
Pennsylvania.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.460
And this, the vaccine itself,

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:57.660
the end product of medicine's long match with
measles.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:16.040
[Music]

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.020
[Narrator:] Many parents think of measles
as just a common nuisance,

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:26.090
which makes their children feel miserable
and keeps them out of school for a while.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:30.240
But physicians today know that measles is
more than a nuisance.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.710
It can bring on bacterial infections,

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:36.630
can cause fatal pneumonia, and in some cases
encephalitis,

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.750
inflammation of the brain.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.820
Each case needs good medical care.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.670
It is not so much because of the usual rash
and fever symptoms of measles

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:48.590
that the doctor says he'll check back in a
day or so,

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:55.790
but rather to be sure the young patient is
not developing serious complications.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:59.890
Electroencephalograms indicate that half the
patients with natural measles

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:03.600
show some brain involvement during the disease.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.260
After the disease has passed, most patients,

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:10.030
such as this boy being tested in Philadelphia's
Children's Hospital,

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.280
show a return to a normal brain wave pattern,

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:18.510
a distinct contrast to the abnormal pattern
recorded during the disease.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:24.069
Still, in those patients who showed the abnormal
encephalogram during their illness,

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:27.439
the possibility of future emotional instability,

00:02:27.439 --> 00:02:32.310
or mental deficiency, or even mental retardation,
cannot be ruled out.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:38.709
Fortunately, only about one measles patient
in a thousand develops encephalitis.

00:02:38.709 --> 00:02:42.900
As of this time, measles is by far our most
serious epidemic childhood disease.

00:02:43.389 --> 00:02:46.540
Although nearly half a million cases are reported
each year,

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.889
the actual number is probably closer to four
million.

00:02:50.889 --> 00:02:57.280
In 1961, after the polio vaccines had reduced
the deaths from that disease to 90,

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.019
that same year, 434 measles deaths were reported.

00:03:05.279 --> 00:03:07.469
In the less developed countries of the world,

00:03:07.469 --> 00:03:10.499
the toll taken by measles is much greater.

00:03:10.499 --> 00:03:16.189
In Nigeria it is estimated that one out of
four babies contracting measles dies from it.

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:22.840
The tragic toll of measles is also told in
a neighboring republic, Upper Volta,

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:31.819
where in one village an epidemic killed 113
out of 115 children who got the disease.

00:03:31.819 --> 00:03:33.709
Across the ocean in Chile,

00:03:33.709 --> 00:03:39.090
measles accounts for half of all childhood
deaths from acute communicable diseases each year.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.459
Thus now, as it has for centuries past,

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:49.659
measles takes its toll of human life.

00:03:49.659 --> 00:03:52.230
It was a Persian physician named Rhazes

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:56.810
who gave the first classical description of
measles ten centuries ago.

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:59.959
He and other Arabian physicians first suggested
that measles

00:03:59.959 --> 00:04:02.629
is a distinct and separate disease.

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:06.189
It had often been considered a form of the
pox.

00:04:06.189 --> 00:04:08.620
But these early doctors described and treated

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:12.280
the symptoms of the disease, not the cause.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.010
There were many remedies but no prevention.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.609
The cause remained a mystery.

00:04:17.609 --> 00:04:20.650
Then, in the eighteenth century,

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:24.830
the light began to dawn on some of the causes
of infectious disease.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:33.780
Jenner of England, Pasteur of France, Koch
of Germany, founded the science of bacteriology.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:36.620
With improved microscopes came the microbe
hunters.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.330
They identified bacteria, grew them,

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:43.370
and experimented with them in their laboratories.

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:47.400
Their search pointed the way to discovery
of another disease agent,

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.720
a millimicrobe, the virus,

00:04:49.729 --> 00:04:55.729
and to the development of a new medical research
specialty, virology.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:00.009
At hospitals and research centers today,

00:05:00.009 --> 00:05:04.060
virology is a major and growing scientific
discipline.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:07.430
And in a laboratory attached to Children's
Hospital in Boston,

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:10.710
is one of the nation's most respected virologists,

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:15.669
Harvard scientist and Nobel Prize winner Dr. John Enders.

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:21.780
In 1953, a few years after Dr. Enders' work
paved the way for the polio vaccines,

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:25.090
he and his team turned their attention to
measles.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:31.639
The first objective: to find and to grow the
measles virus.

00:05:31.639 --> 00:05:36.080
Blood samples taken by Dr. Thomas Peebles
from children with natural measles

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:42.000
were injected into cultures of human kidney
cells and incubated.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.300
With techniques like these being carried out
today by Dr. Samuel Katz,

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.610
tissue cultures brought from the incubator

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:52.949
are checked for any changes in the cells.

00:05:52.949 --> 00:05:57.060
Obtaining even one successful growth of pure
virulent measles virus

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:00.550
is one of the most difficult laboratory achievements.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:06.540
Finally, in 1954, one culture obtained from
an 11-year old measles patient

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:11.420
named David Edmonston begins to show remarkable changes in cell structure.

00:06:12.539 --> 00:06:17.009
These might be caused by the measles virus.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:24.280
Dr. Enders is called in to observe it.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.409
To prove that it is the measles virus, they
decide to inject it,

00:06:28.409 --> 00:06:30.530
as Dr. Katz demonstrates here,

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:35.250
into the only animal that will contract the
disease--monkeys.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:41.030
Monkeys which have never been exposed to measles.

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:43.669
In a few days, when the monkey develops measles,

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:49.429
they know they have isolated and grown the
Edmonston strain of the measles virus.

00:06:50.919 --> 00:06:54.229
Now they discuss the longest, and in many
ways the most difficult,

00:06:54.229 --> 00:06:58.199
task of all, how to attenuate or weaken the virus

00:06:58.199 --> 00:07:01.759
so that it will produce antibodies and thus
provide immunity

00:07:01.759 --> 00:07:04.009
without transmitting the disease itself.

00:07:04.009 --> 00:07:09.620
It's a little like walking on a tightrope.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:15.069
The virus is grown first in one tissue culture,
then in another.

00:07:15.069 --> 00:07:26.590
Human kidney tissues, human amnion, egg amnion,
chick embryo.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:31.330
It is transferred.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:33.199
It is incubated.

00:07:33.199 --> 00:07:39.110
Always carefully watched and safeguarded against
bacterial infection at every stage.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:42.900
As the weeks pass, the virus makes 72 passages in all,

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:46.469
before Dr. Enders decides it's ready for the
next tests

00:07:46.469 --> 00:07:49.769
with experimental animals.

00:07:50.729 --> 00:07:52.819
Two groups of monkeys are used.

00:07:52.819 --> 00:07:58.379
One group is given the attenuated virus as
a vaccine.

00:07:58.379 --> 00:08:00.159
The other group is not vaccinated.

00:08:00.159 --> 00:08:05.150
Later, both groups are given the full-strength
measles virus.

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:07.770
In a few weeks the results are evident.

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:11.310
The monkeys that were not vaccinated developed
measles.

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:16.499
The ones like this one that were given the
experimental vaccine show no signs of measles,

00:08:16.499 --> 00:08:19.150
but they have developed protective antibodies.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:24.319
Dr. Enders and Dr. Katz now know that they
have developed for the first time

00:08:24.319 --> 00:08:30.280
a vaccine which will provide safe protection
against measles.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:35.060
It only remains to test the attenuated live
virus vaccine with humans.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:37.340
Starting first with children at a state school,

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:42.529
Dr. Katz then inoculates volunteers who come
to his lab at the hospital.

00:08:42.529 --> 00:08:44.430
The results are most encouraging

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:52.370
and spark interest throughout the world of
virology.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:55.380
One who saw the importance of moving forward
with this breakthrough

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:59.310
was Dr. Maurice Hilleman, Director of Virus
and Cell Biology

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:04.839
at the Merck Sharp and Dohme Research Laboratories
in West Point, Pennsylvania.

00:09:04.839 --> 00:09:08.279
With cultures of attenuated virus from Dr.
Enders' lab,

00:09:08.279 --> 00:09:11.720
Dr. Hilleman, Dr. Eugene Buynak, and colleagues

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:15.149
undertake development of larger experimental
quantities.

00:09:15.149 --> 00:09:17.850
At the same time, Dr. Hilleman draws up the design

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:24.410
of the next critical step--broadscale clinical testing.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:30.589
Collaborating with Dr. Hilleman is a group
at Children's Hospital, Philadelphia,

00:09:30.589 --> 00:09:36.110
headed by Dr. Joseph Stokes, nationally known
pediatrician and medical scientist.

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:42.620
Here with him, Doctors Robert E. Weibel, J.
Ronald Halenda, and Charles M. Riley

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:50.300
map out a plan for field trials in southeastern
Pennsylvania.

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:56.459
More than fifteen hundred children and their
parents cooperate.

00:09:56.459 --> 00:10:00.399
One group of children receives the live vaccine
by injection.

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:03.999
The trial also studies how gamma globulin,
given in the other arm,

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.660
modifies reactions to the vaccine.

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:12.040
Another set of children, for comparison, receives injections

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:15.339
that do not contain the live vaccine.

00:10:15.339 --> 00:10:18.820
A blood sample taken from each child before
vaccination

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:22.480
tells which children have not previously had
the disease.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:28.920
These samples are analyzed in the research laboratory.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.440
Another sample taken four weeks later

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:38.240
shows whether the child has developed antibodies
to the vaccine.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.779
Then, over the next year or so, a close check is kept

00:10:40.779 --> 00:10:44.420
to see if any of the children contract the
real disease.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:47.699
The results fulfill all expectations.

00:10:47.699 --> 00:10:49.949
The vaccinated children are protected.

00:10:49.949 --> 00:10:53.899
None of them get measles when exposed to it.

00:10:53.899 --> 00:10:58.440
From New York University, Dr. Saul Krugman
reports similar findings,

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.779
as does Dr. Fred McCrumb at the University
of Maryland.

00:11:01.779 --> 00:11:04.209
The trials spread across the country.

00:11:04.209 --> 00:11:09.310
The vaccine is tested in 18 states from the
eastern seaboard to California.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:12.630
As the data from all these field trials accumulate,

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.829
answers to earlier questions emerge.

00:11:14.829 --> 00:11:18.740
The live measles vaccine is producing a high
level of immunity,

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:25.910
safely, consistently, and the immunity appears
to be long-lasting.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:30.440
Answers are also emerging on the problems
of large-scale production and quality control,

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:38.660
as manufacture gets underway in the biological
laboratories at West Point, Pennsylvania.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:43.680
The less-developed countries in Africa watch
this progress with great interest.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:48.540
Helping them launch studies of the vaccine
are first, the U.S. Armed Forces Epidemiological Board,

00:11:49.339 --> 00:11:55.659
and later the World Health Organization and U.S Public Health Service.

00:11:57.250 --> 00:12:00.600
It was to the National Institutes of Health
in 1962

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:06.010
that an urgent request came from one of these
African nations.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:13.320
Upper Volta, satisfied with preliminary testing,
asks for a massive vaccination effort.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:17.730
"Help us protect our children before measles
strikes again."

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:21.920
Begun in time, it could save thousands of
lives.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.699
The response is immediate.

00:12:23.699 --> 00:12:27.660
To help train local teams and study the immunization
of this population,

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:32.579
the Public Health Service sends a medical
team from its Division of Biologic Standards.

00:12:32.579 --> 00:12:37.070
Vehicles are supplied by the Agency for International Development.

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:42.030
The vaccine is contributed by Merck Sharp and Dohme.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:44.800
The drum speaks to the people.

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:48.600
"Come to the village, the doctors are here
with the medicine.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:52.269
It can protect your children."

00:12:52.269 --> 00:12:55.040
And the people do come, bringing their children,

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.860
bringing their hopes and fears.

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:06.480
At each village, the jet inoculator used is
carefully explained.

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:14.980
Then begins the long hard job of giving the
lifesaving vaccine to the children.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:22.440
As soon as one village has been protected,
the team must move onto the next.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:27.440
Everywhere, they are greeted by huge crowds.

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:36.509
The vaccine must be kept refrigerated to protect
it from the intense African heat.

00:13:36.509 --> 00:13:44.509
At each new location the inoculator is cleaned
and checked.

00:13:44.509 --> 00:13:48.329
The lines seem endless.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.840
But all the children must get the vaccine.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:57.540
Village after village, the people come by
the thousands.

00:13:57.550 --> 00:14:02.759
The team works around the clock.

00:14:02.759 --> 00:14:04.740
At last the work is done.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:09.459
By March 1963, 700,000 children in Upper Volta

00:14:09.459 --> 00:14:12.720
receive live-virus measles vaccine.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:16.940
Many thousands of lives may have been saved.

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:20.000
That same month, the Department of Health,
Education, and Welfare

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.769
licenses the vaccine for general use in the
United States.

00:14:23.769 --> 00:14:27.309
The Surgeon General of the United States Public Health Service, Dr. Luther Terry,

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:29.820
has this to say.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:35.120
[Dr. Terry:] Over the past several years,
measles vaccines have been successfully tested

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:37.850
both in this country and abroad.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:43.819
This painstaking evaluation was made possible
by the cooperative effort of scientists,

00:14:43.819 --> 00:14:49.199
both in and out of government, by physicians,
by the drug industry,

00:14:49.199 --> 00:14:53.120
and by thousands of unselfish and courageous
parents

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:57.959
who have permitted their children to participate
in the field trials.

00:14:57.959 --> 00:15:00.379
The Secretary of Health, Education, and Welfare

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:03.700
has now licensed the vaccines for general use.

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:09.180
As increasing numbers of children are vaccinated, we will be well on the way

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:12.380
to eradicating a disease that down through
the centuries

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:19.430
has killed millions of children and left others impaired mentally and physically.

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:23.950
All of those who have contributed in any way to this cause for better health

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:27.840
can be proud of a great achievement.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:33.560
[Narrator:] Within 48 hours of official government
licensing,

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:39.259
supplies of the vaccine are ready for shipment
to doctors throughout the country.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:45.040
Today, production of the vaccine is in full
swing, protected at each step

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:51.950
by the elaborate manufacturing controls established
by industry, together with the federal government.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:58.500
Production of the live virus vaccine begins
with fertile chicken eggs.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:04.069
To assure absolute purity, the eggs are taken from select, disease-free chickens

00:16:04.069 --> 00:16:08.850
kept in strict sanitary isolation.

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:13.509
The eggs are opened and the embryos are carefully
removed.

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:24.600
They are minced and washed, then further broken down by a chemical substance

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:27.899
that reduces the tissue to individual cells.

00:16:27.899 --> 00:16:33.839
It is only in living cells that the virus can grow.

00:16:33.839 --> 00:16:38.810
To keep these cells alive and growing, a special
nutrient is prepared.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:44.319
A precise number of cells is counted and introduced
into each bottle.

00:16:44.319 --> 00:16:47.610
Then the measles virus is introduced.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:50.560
Eighty percent of the culture bottles are
infected.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:53.139
The other 20 percent are used as controls.

00:16:53.139 --> 00:16:58.420
They provide a way to check against any possible
impurities in the cells.

00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:01.139
The cells attach themselves to the walls,

00:17:01.139 --> 00:17:07.020
and in the infected bottles the virus grows
in the cells.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:11.530
Now begins a three-week period in which the
nutrient is periodically replaced.

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:16.850
The cells are rinsed and the growth is carefully
watched.

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:29.559
The fluid now taken from the culture bottles
contains a high concentration of measles virus.

00:17:29.559 --> 00:17:31.830
The individual harvests are pooled together.

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:36.600
Also, a stabilizer is added and samples are
removed for testing.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:39.980
Finally, the entire pool of vaccine is filtered.

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:45.870
This, at last, is the pure live virus vaccine.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:58.190
It is frozen at minus 75 degrees to await
results of final testing.

00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:02.480
It takes 137 days to produce the vaccine.

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:07.590
Ninety-six of these are devoted to meticulous
quality control testing.

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:11.030
More than 35 separate tests are performed
to ensure

00:18:11.030 --> 00:18:15.309
potency, safety, and other measures of quality
control.

00:18:15.309 --> 00:18:19.159
For each person involved in the actual production
of the vaccine,

00:18:19.159 --> 00:18:24.890
eight people devote their time to testing
and control.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:30.480
Finally, the vaccine which has passed all
of the tests

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:34.240
is thawed and transferred to individual bottles.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:40.159
These are then freeze-dried, capped, and sealed.

00:18:40.159 --> 00:18:46.549
The end result is a single-dose vial of the
live, attenuated-virus measles vaccine.

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:53.820
But the real story of a vaccine is told in
the fears and smiles of a little girl

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.830
who today is given greater protection than
ever before

00:18:56.830 --> 00:19:00.679
against the infectious diseases of childhood.

00:19:00.679 --> 00:19:04.759
There remain other viruses to be isolated,
other vaccines to come,

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:06.760
but they will.

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:08.600
And like this little girl,

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:15.660
millions of children over the world will have
an even safer and healthier life.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:46.820
[Music]

